cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "EAP Skill Taxonomy"
abstract: >-
  An open, graph-structured taxonomy of English for Academic Purposes:
  569 micro-topics across 16 strands and 51 domains, a prerequisite
  dependency graph, research-informed teaching guidance for every topic,
  alignment to CEFR Companion Volume scales, IELTS criteria, the ACRL
  Framework and the Vitae Researcher Development Framework, and a
  citation-backed bibliography. Covers foundation, pre-sessional,
  in-sessional (undergraduate and taught postgraduate) and doctoral
  contexts, general and discipline-specific EAP.
type: dataset
version: "v1"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
repository-code: "https://github.com/henders23/eap-prereq"
keywords:
  - English for academic purposes
  - EAP
  - academic literacy
  - curriculum
  - prerequisite graph
  - CEFR
authors:
  - name: "EAP Skill Taxonomy contributors"
